"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7\",\"title\":\"A Biochar Project at Satyapura — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"BICRS\",\"200Y+\",\"A Biochar Project at Satyapura\",\"Equilibrium\",\"ISSUED\",\"1.47\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"0.03\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"27 Nov 2025 to 26 Nov 2030\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"1.47\",\"buffer_header\":\"0.03\",\"crediting\":\"27 Nov 2025 to 26 Nov 2030\",\"verifier\":\"Enviance\",\"code\":\"TS26\",\"approval\":\"30 Jan 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"1.47\",\"cert_retired\":\"0\",\"cert_buffer\":\"0.03\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Equilibrium's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.03 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.03 certificates.\\n\\nEquilibrium has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\",\"Showing 5 of 7\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Name\",\"Category\",\"Validated\"],\"rows\":[[\"Prosopis juliflora - v1.3\",\"Biomass\",\"02 Feb 2026\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"Validation and Verification Report (updated)\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"GHG Statement\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"Exemption Note\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"23 Dec 2025\",\"Project Name Change Record\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"1.47\",\"0.03\",\"1.44\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66\",\"t\":\"Equilibrium\"},{\"h\":\"https://enviance.in\",\"t\":\"Enviance\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KGQX6MRZ1S0MRT2/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 30 Jan 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KCVY3QC71S03X21?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KYVWQE7F1S02JZ0/validation_and_verification_report_%28updated%29.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KGQX6MRZ1S0MRT2/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KG78WF7H1S0YA48/ghg_statement.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KG78TWQG1S0Q0CY/exemption_note.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1K3VWSDS61S0QKV7/pjd_1KD62QHEP1S0NNC6/project_name_change_record.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nA Biochar Project at Satyapura\\nEquilibrium\\nISSUED\\n1.47\\nBUFFER POOL\\n0.03\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n27 Nov 2025 to 26 Nov 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThe Biochar Project at Satyapura, in Rajasthan, India transforms invasive Prosopis juliflora into durable biochar, beginning at 10 TPD and scaling to 50 TPD. In the second phase, the project will consider using agri-residue feedstocks such as mustard husk, castor and cotton-stalks which will be validated against Isometric's Biomass Protocol. By diverting biomass from decay and combustion, the project locks carbon away for the long term while improving soils, reducing emissions, and supporting rural livelihoods. Every step of the process is digitally monitored and independently verified, ensuring full transparency. The project takes its name from the historic region of Sanchore in western Rajasthan - once known as Satyapura, or the “city of truth.” In this spirit, it draws on ancestral wisdom and nature-based practices that honor the soil, the community, and the climate. By converting waste biomass into biochar, Satyapura restores degraded land, enriches soil organic carbon, and uplifts rural communities. At its heart, the project is about returning to the land’s truth - quietly and powerfully regenerating from what it has always known.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nEnviance\\n->\\nProject code\\nTS26\\nApproval date\\n30 Jan 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nA Biochar Project at Satyapura\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n30 Jan 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 0.74 tCO₂e removed from A Biochar Project at Satyapura on 10 Dec 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n736 kg\\nSequestrations\\n940 kg\\n-\\nActivities\\n203 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nProsopis juliflora - v1.3\\tBiomass\\t02 Feb 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n30 Jan 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report (updated)\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Jan 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Jan 2026\\tGHG Statement\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Jan 2026\\tExemption Note\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n23 Dec 2025\\tProject Name Change Record\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 7\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n1.47\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n0.03\\nCrediting period\\n27 Nov 2025 to 26 Nov 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n30 Jan 2026\\t1.47\\t0.03\\t1.44\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Equilibrium's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.03 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.03 certificates.\\n\\nEquilibrium has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"